Lane files edited OUTSIDE rowt since its last logged state — by hand, or by an
agent writing the file directly, the case that used to leave no trace at all.

config/cache/lane-state.tsv is the last state rowt logged. It disagrees with the
base fixture's lane files in four ways:
  * ads.example is in block-domains.txt but not in the state  -> an outside ADD
  * gone.example is in the state's escape lane, in no file     -> an outside REMOVAL
  * tracker.example.net is block in the files, escape in the state -> an outside MOVE
  * domain:not-a-dup.example is an EXACT entry only the state holds -> an outside
    REMOVAL spelled the way the file spelled it, `domain:` and all

The next mutating command, or the next watchdog tick, has to log exactly those
as `LANE outside rowt: …` BEFORE its own BEGIN — never blamed on the command —
and then adopt the live state. host.pid.self makes the router read as running,
so a `watch tick` reaches its corp sync, the step that runs the check in a tick.
